{# The README's "At a glance" box: the headline figures of the validation report, rendered by the same pass and from the
   same context (report/validation.py `render_glance`), each with its evaluation label as the report prints it, and
   written between the README's two markers (`write_glance`); the stamp holds its hash. Each row says what the report
   says, from the same branches and the same macros: the status follows the 2025 test of record, and the 2025 row
   appears once that test has finished (before, the status says where it stands). The caveats go once, under the
   table. English only, as the README is. #}
{% from 'sentences.en.md.j2' import status_line, withdrawn, label, span, recs, bias_limit, coverage_line, VERDICT, OUTCOME %}
{% set prod, fam, ship = sel.models.production, sel.models.family, sel.models.shipped %}
{% set vy = K.validation_years %}
{% set HY = K.held_out_year %}
{% set R = held.record if held else none %}
{% set finished = R is not none and R.finished %}
{% set LR = limits.replay %}
{% set n_recs = r.summary.recommendations.values()|sum %}
{% set controls = b.breaks|selectattr('control')|list %}
{% set tests = b.breaks|rejectattr('control')|list %}
{% set not_better = r.verdict.shipped in ('not_shown_better', 'worse') or r.verdict.family in ('not_shown_better', 'worse') %}
> **At a glance.** Rendered by `valiwatt report`: every measured value comes from the tracked runs, every design constant from the runs or the code, and each result carries its evaluation label as the validation report prints it.
>
> {{ status_line(status, R, say, vy, r.year, HY) }}{% if recommendation %} The claims this result touches are withdrawn: {{ withdrawn(recommendation.withdrawn) }}. Recommendation to the owner, in the monitor's form: **{{ say.recommendation[recommendation.kind] }}**; the model in use next is his decision.{% endif +%}
>
> | | |
> |---|---|
> | **Validation, {{ span(vy) }}** ({{ label(v.contrasts.label) }}) | MAPE {{ sel.mape[prod]|pct(2) }} for v2, {{ sel.mape[fam]|pct(2) }} for v1's form on the same forecast, {{ sel.mape[ship]|pct(2) }} for v1 as shipped, over {{ sel.hours|num }} common hours. {{ coverage_line(nominal, C.relative.overall.mean, v.conformal.first_fold, sides, v.folds.last, "v2's") }} |
> | **{{ r.year }} replay** ({{ label(r.contrasts.label) }}) | MAPE {{ r.summary.mape.mean|pct(2) }}, coverage {{ r.summary.coverage.mean|pct(1) }}, {{ recs(n_recs) }}. Verdicts against v1 as shipped / against v1's form: "{{ VERDICT[r.verdict.shipped] }}" / "{{ VERDICT[r.verdict.family] }}". |
{% if finished %}
> | **{{ HY }}** ({{ label(R.evaluation) }}) | Test of record `{{ R.run_id }}`, standing "{{ OUTCOME[R.standing] }}". Verdicts against v1 as shipped / against v1's form: "{{ VERDICT[R.verdict.shipped] }}" / "{{ VERDICT[R.verdict.family] }}". |
{% endif %}
> | **What the monitor can miss** | On {{ r.year }} ({{ label(r.contrasts.label) }}), {{ bias_limit(LR, K.power_horizon) }}. |
> | **Checks** | {{ tests|selectattr('outcome', 'equalto', 'passed')|list|length }} of {{ tests|length }} breaks passed, {{ controls|selectattr('outcome', 'equalto', 'passed')|list|length }} of {{ controls|length }} controls stayed quiet (synthetic data). Rules frozen at tag `{{ freeze.freeze_tag }}`{% if departures %}, now at commit `{{ freeze.freeze_commit|short }}` after a departure recorded in `AGENTS.md`{% else %}, commit `{{ freeze.freeze_commit|short }}`{% endif %}. |
> | **Read next** | The story, read first: [French](docs/report/story.fr.md), the reference; [English](docs/report/story.en.md). The full validation report: [French](docs/report/validation.fr.md); [English](docs/report/validation.en.md). |
>
> {{ r.year }} is not a test: the developers had seen it through v1 before choosing v2{% if not_better %}, and a verdict that is not "better" there is a finding against v2{% else %}, so it supports no claim{% endif %}{% if departures %}; replayed again after a departure from v2's frozen rules, it is post hoc{% endif %}. The breaks run on synthetic data: a break shows that a check can fire, not that it would see the same fault in real demand.
